ished descriptions and the ground file's OpenStreetMap outlines, not photographs (none reachable): the palace stood about 14 m north of its outline, so it was moved 14 m south and 2 m west onto it (on 45% before, 63% now; the outline's eastern half is shallower than the western, which a symmetrical palace cannot follow, so no further shift was taken); the roofs and domes, drawn grey-green, are now in the copper-green of the real roofs; the south forecourt widened and the great pond drawn back to the site's south edge, where the outlines show it begins (most of it lies beyond the plate); the gate lodges moved to the forecourt. Still guessed: the heights, the window rhythm, the garden parterres."}